    Case 2: s ≢ 0 (mod p)
    Then P = (s³ - k) · inv(2s) (mod p)
    Elements a[i], a[j] with sum s and product P are roots of quadratic:
    t² - s·t + P ≡ 0 (mod p)
    Discriminant D = s² - 4P = s² - 2(s³ - k)/s = s - 2 + 2k/s (mod p)
    Roots exist if D is quadratic residue.

    Optimal approach for k = 0: count pairs with sum ≡ 0
    For k ≠ 0: O(n²) approach is simplest and will work for smaller test cases
    '''
